  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/coderdailyone/dsh-plugin-browser-use/main/docs/assets/banner.svg\" alt=\"dsh-plugin-browser-use — a real browser for the DeepSeek Harness, fenced by a security-first policy\" width=\"100%\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-plugin-browser-use\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/dsh-plugin-browser-use?color=6366f1&label=npm\" alt=\"npm version\"></a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/coderdailyone/dsh-plugin-browser-use/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/coderdailyone/dsh-plugin-browser-use/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"CI\"></a>\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/node/v/dsh-plugin-browser-use?color=818cf8\" alt=\"node version\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/l/dsh-plugin-browser-use?color=22d3ee\" alt=\"license\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"#install\">Install</a> · <a href=\"#the-tools\">Tools</a> · <a href=\"#security-model\">Security model</a> · <a href=\"#configuration\">Configuration</a> · <a href=\"./README.zh.md\">中文文档</a>\n</p>\n\nA [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/dsh) plugin that gives the model a real browser — navigate, click, fill, read, screenshot, tabs, downloads — backed by Chromium through `playwright-core`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "Its differentiator is a **security-first design**: every URL is re-checked against a host-label allowlist and a private-network block **on every action and again after every navigation** — including redirects, link clicks, popups, background loads, and downloads. And no tool ever accepts a filesystem path from the model: every file the plugin writes lands in a constrained directory under a name the plugin picked itself."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-browser-use\ndsh --profile web --dump-config   # should show the \"# == dsh-plugin-browser-use\" layer\n```\n\nA Chromium is required. The plugin resolves one in this order:\n\n1. `executablePath` config\n2. `$DSH_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE`\n3. Well-known OS locations (Chrome / Chromium / Edge / Brave)\n4. Playwright's own browser resolution (`npx playwright install chromium`)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "| key | type | default | meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `allowedHosts` | `string[]` | `[]` | Host-label allowlist. `example.com` matches `example.com` and `*.example.com`; matching is on host labels, never substrings. Empty = any public host. |\n| `allowPrivateNetwork` | `boolean` | `false` | Permit loopback / private / link-local targets. Off by default. |\n| `headless` | `boolean` | `true` | Run without a window. |\n| `executablePath` | `string` | — | Explicit Chromium binary. Falls back to `$DSH_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE`, OS locations, then Playwright. |\n| `userAgent` | `string` | `dsh-plugin-browser-use/<version>` | User-Agent for the browser context. |\n| `proxyServer` | `string` | — | Proxy for browser traffic (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:7890`, `socks5://…`). Chromium ignores `$http_proxy`-style env, so set this (or `$DSH_BROWSER_PROXY`) on machines that need a proxy. |\n| `proxyBypass` | `string` | — | Comma-separated hosts that bypass the proxy. |\n| `navigationTimeoutMs` | `int ≥ 1` | `30000` | Page-load budget per navigation. |\n| `actionTimeoutMs` | `int ≥ 1` | `15000` | Budget per click / fill / read / screenshot. |\n| `maxTextChars` | `int ≥ 1` | `20000` | Hard bound on extracted"
    },
    {
      "section": "The tools",
      "text": "| tool | model-facing result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `browser_navigate` | `{ url, title, statusCode, text, truncated }` of the landed page |\n| `browser_navigate_background` | `{ jobId, index, url }` — loads in a new unfocused tab as a background job |\n| `browser_click` | `{ url, title, text, truncated }` after the click's navigation settles |\n| `browser_fill` | `{ url, title }` after filling a field |\n| `browser_read_text` | `{ url, title, text, truncated }` re-read of the current page |\n| `browser_read_snapshot` | `{ url, title, snapshot, truncated }` — aria role/name outline, selector-stable |\n| `browser_screenshot` | `{ path, url, title }` — PNG under `artifactsDir`, plugin-named |\n| `browser_pdf` | `{ path, url, title }` — PDF under `artifactsDir` (headless only) |\n| `browser_downloads` | `{ downloads: [{ index, url, suggestedFilename, state, path?, error? }] }` |\n| `browser_upload` | `{ url, title }` — attach a file from `uploadsDir` to an `<input type=file>` |\n| `browser_tab_new` | `{ index, url, title, statusCode? }` — new active tab, policy-checked before creation |\n| `browser_tab_list` | `{ tabs: [{ index, active, url, allowed, title? }] }` |\n| `browser_tab_select` | `{ index, u"
    },
    {
      "section": "The tools",
      "text": "Each agent session owns an isolated browser with an ordered tab list; calls from one owner are serialized in submission order (`browser_navigate_background` is the deliberate exception — its load runs outside the queue). All failures surface as ordinary `isError` tool results with a `BROWSER_*` code (never a thrown exception), e.g. `BROWSER_HOST_NOT_ALLOWED`, `BROWSER_PRIVATE_NETWORK`, `BROWSER_NO_PAGE`, `BROWSER_NO_SUCH_TAB`, `BROWSER_UPLOAD_NOT_ALLOWED`, `BROWSER_JOBS_UNAVAILABLE`, `BROWSER_NAVIGATION_FAILED`, `BROWSER_ACTION_FAILED`, `BROWSER_LAUNCH_FAILED`, `BROWSER_CLOSED`, `BROWSER_ABORTED`, `BROWSER_UNSUPPORTED_SCHEME`, `BROWSER_INVALID_URL`."
    },
    {
      "section": "The tools",
      "text": "Background loads need the jobs registry (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-jobs` + `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-jobs`) in the profile; without it the tool fails closed with `BROWSER_JOBS_UNAVAILABLE`. Jobs register under kind `browser`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security model",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/coderdailyone/dsh-plugin-browser-use/main/docs/assets/policy-loop.svg\" alt=\"The policy loop: checked before every action, re-checked after every landing; refusals never reach the model\" width=\"100%\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Security model",
      "text": "- **Continuous re-check.** The policy runs before every action, and again after every navigation — `browser_navigate` checks the *landed* URL, so a redirect (or a link click) that crosses into a disallowed host is refused even when the requested URL was allowed. Background loads get the same pre-flight and post-landing checks.\n- **Host-label matching, never substrings.** `allowedHosts: [\"example.com\"]` matches `example.com` and `sub.example.com` but **not** `evil-example.com` or `evil.example.com.attacker.test`.\n- **Private networks blocked by default.** Loopback, private, link-local, unique-local, and IPv4-mapped spellings (`127.0.0.1`, `10.0.0.5`, `::1`, `::ffff:127.0.0.1`, `fc00::/7` hex forms, …) are refused unless `allowPrivateNetwork` is explicitly enabled — and when an allowlist is set, private hosts must be on it too.\n- **Canonical host comparison.** Case, trailing dots, and IPv6 brackets are normalized before comparison; anything unparseable fails closed.\n- **Scheme restriction.** Only `http:` and `https:` navigate; `file:`, `data:`, `javascript:`, and other schemes are refused outright.\n- **No model-controlled paths, ever.** Screenshots, PDFs, and downloads are written on"
    },
    {
      "section": "Model Experience",
      "text": "**What the model sees:** fifteen `browser_*` tool names; navigation and reads return the landed URL, title, HTTP status (navigation only), and bounded visible text or an aria outline. Screenshots/PDFs return paths, not image payloads — pair with an attachment-capable setup to show them to a vision model."
    },
    {
      "section": "Model Experience",
      "text": "**Token effect:** each navigate / read / snapshot returns up to `maxTextChars` (default 20,000) characters; shrink it for cheaper sessions, grow it for dense pages. Click returns a fresh reading; fill, tab, and artifact tools return only small fixed shapes.\n\n**KV cache effect:** none — results are ordinary tool results appended to the conversation; nothing rewrites the prompt prefix."
    },
    {
      "section": "Known limitations and deferred work",
      "text": "- DNS rebinding not defended; refused redirects still cost one outbound request (see Security model).\n- Screenshots/PDFs are saved as files, not returned as image content — wiring them into `ctx.attachments` for vision models is future work.\n- Cookie persistence is a single storage-state file: last close wins across concurrent agents.\n- Playwright's `goto` cannot be interrupted mid-flight: cancelling a background job marks it and the navigation timeout bounds settlement.\n- `playwright-core` needs a browser binary present (see Install).\n- dsh is a developer preview; expect lockstep peer-version bumps."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run build    # tsc → lib/\nnpm test         # vitest run (96 tests; live smoke self-skips)\n```\n\nThe live smoke suite runs a real Chromium when `DSH_BROWSER_LIVE=1` and a browser resolves (set `DSH_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE` to pin one):\n\n```bash\nDSH_BROWSER_LIVE=1 npm test\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Layout: `src/policy.ts` (pure URL policy) → `src/session.ts` (browser session: tabs, artifacts, downloads, per-action re-checks) → `src/tool.ts` (dsh tool definitions, owner registry) → `src/index.ts` (plugin entry). CI runs typecheck + the keyless suite on Node 22/24."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    },
    {
      "section": "Non-affiliation",
      "text": "This project is **not affiliated with the [browser-use](https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use) project or company**. Under the hood it drives Chromium directly through `playwright-core`; no browser-use code is involved."
    }
